+H1, +H1.1, +H1.1.1, +H1.1.2, +H1.1.3, +H1.2, +H1.2.1, +H1.3, +H1.3.1, +H1.4, +H1.4.1, +H1.5, +H1.5.1, +H2, +H2.1, +H2.1.1, +H2.2, +H2.2.1, +H2.3, +H2.3.1, +H3, +H3.1, +H3.1.1, +H3.2, +H3.2.1, +H4, +H4.1, +H4.1.1, +H4.2, +H4.2.1. The tree was empty and there are no results yet, so I seeded it with 4 open Lvl1 hypotheses. H1: sample efficiency, i.e. the number of epochs needed. It covers the airbench96-style base without TTA, Muon at batch size about 2000, label smoothing 0.3, proxy-model hard-example selection, and widening the last block. H2: per-step GPU throughput, covering compile, channels_last and half precision done in build, a fused optimizer with a compiled step, and progressive resizing. H3: fixed overheads in the timed region, covering keeping data on the GPU, augmenting on the GPU, and compiling every shape in build. H4: variance and the noise floor against the 3-seed 0.753 cutoff, covering rerun spread and lookahead/EMA. Each Lvl2 has a numeric Lvl3 prediction. Planned order: (1) run the untouched template as E001; (2) test H1.1.1 and H1.1.2 with an epoch sweep (H1.1.3) to find the knee; (3) run repeats for the noise floor (H4.1.1) before claiming any improvement; (4) then apply the systems levers (H2, H3) and Muon (H1.2). Watch the rules: no TTA, and no real data in build.
added I001, I002, I003, I004, I005, I006, I007, I008; dropped none. So far there is only the harness smoke test (E000: chance accuracy, ~0.1 s fixed overhead per trial), so the queue opens with a real recipe. The top idea (H1.1.1, priority 5) is an airbench96-style net without TTA at 10 epochs, with data and augmentation on the GPU and compile done in build(). It is expected to land at about 0.758 accuracy in 9-14 s. Two ideas then map the epoch knee (H1.1.2 at 8.5 epochs, H1.1.3 at 9 or 11 epochs). A rerun of the base measures the noise floor (H4.1.1). Two single-change ablations follow: label smoothing 0.2 vs 0.3 (H1.3.1) and removing lookahead (H4.2.1). The last two are explore bets: Muon on the conv filters (H1.2.1) and progressive resizing (H2.3.1). The queue was empty, so nothing is dropped.
